Source: ps3-boot
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: PS3 Linux project <ps3@localhost>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ps3-boot
Architecture: all
Depends: linux-base, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Petitboot boot menu for the PS3 from the installed kernels
 ps3-update-kboot writes /etc/kboot.conf, Petitboot's boot menu, with one entry per kernel in
 /boot (the newest first and the default). Kernel packages run it through the hooks in
 /usr/share/kernel/postinst.d and postrm.d. The root and extra arguments come from
 /etc/default/ps3-boot, each kernel's own from /usr/lib/ps3/boot/<release>.args. Extra entries
 (e.g. the SSD root's) in /etc/kboot.d/*.conf are appended as written, so kernel installs keep them.
